# Workflow: artefact-ready

This document show to manage artefact packages using artefact-ready facility

## 2. Instructions
- Complete part or full of DAG (makefile) to meet user intent
- Only run a target using **Command** if no dependency found
- If a target has dependencies, make sure all of its dependency targets completed
- If target got failure, do not execute its parent target

## Inventory Directory

| OS Context | Path                            |
| ---------- | ------------------------------- |
| Windows    | `~/echo-home/windows`           |
| Mac OS     | `~/echo-home/workstation/macos` |
| Linux      | `~/echo-home`                   |

## Workflow 

### 1. Deploy a package
```Makefile
inventory:
    # Description: check if <package> exists inventory
    # Command: `cd <inventory_path>; cat .properd/artefacts.yaml | grep <package>`
    # Success: output show `package` name
    # Failure: output show no `package` name, workflow can be aborted immediately
    # Output: <package_name> , <package_version>

check_sum: inventory
    # Description: verify package integrity
    # Command: `.function/artefacts <package_name>`
    # Success: output with `<package_name>-.*: OK`
    # Failure: output without OK` then run workflow `download` and retry
    # Retry: 1
deploy: check_sum
    # Description: install package into system
    # Command: `.function/artefact-readi <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output
    # Input: check_sum must be OK and download is in Success
``` 

### 2. Download a package

```makefile
download: inventory
    # Description: download package
    # Command: `.function/artefact-geti <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output 
    # Input: <package_name>
    # Retry: 1
```
